Confuse yourself, perhaps with a potion.  While you are confused, read a scroll  
of enchant weapon.  The weapon you are wielding, instead of becoming enchanted  
in the usual sense, will be made rust-proof.  No effects that might corrode it  
will work thereafter.

> Is there any easy way of getting it back to +0 or better?

None except using a scroll of enchant weapon.

> Is there any reason for keeping all of the others (they're heavy!)?

Not really.  Some of them give resistance to their special attacks.  The only  
one which isn't obvious is Excalibur, which gives immunity to level drain (as  
does Stormbringer).  Just figure out the one or two which work best for you and  
leave the others somewhere where an orc won't grab it.  (Nothing could be more  
disconcerting than the message "The Uruk-hai swings his broadsword named  
Stormbringer.  -more-")

